sentences.t:
πῶς ἔτλης ἐπὶ νῆας Ἀχαιῶν ἐλθέμεν οἶος
ἀνδρὸς ἐς ὀφθαλμοὺς ὅς τοι πολέας τε καὶ ἐσθλοὺς
υἱέας ἐξενάριξα;

sentences.tr:
pōs etlēs epi nēas Achaiōn elthemen oios
andros es ophthalmous hos toi poleas te kai esthlous
huieas exenarixa;

sentences.l:
But upon him also set a god an evil, that for him not at all
of children in the halls offspring came to be, of ruling ones,
but one child she bore, all-untimely;

“Do not yet seat me on a chair, Zeus-nurtured one, while Hector
lies in the huts uncared for, but as quickly as possible
release him, so that with my eyes I may see;
